--- outbound paths carry no backslashes
pwd clean
PWD clean
pwd == PWD
mktemp clean
realpath clean
--- the value is usable by the shell's own string operations
case-suffix-ok
glob-match-ok
basename-strip=tests
dirname-strip-ok
round-trip-cd-ok
--- SYMMETRY: out then back in is the same string
pwd->cd->pwd stable
realpath agrees with pwd
absolute read ok
abs clean
read from elsewhere ok
--- INBOUND: the MSYS /<d>/... form resolves to the same file
one
msys-form read ok
msys clean
--- IO failures are LOUD, never fatal
split rc=1 (shell alive)
cat rc=1
redirect rc=1
md5sum rc=1
still running after four failures
--- OUTBOUND ONLY: backslash keeps its escape meaning in arguments
 a \t b
0
1
C:\temp
a\b
0
lit\nlit
